{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PdGq1Hck5V1DxeVoLUvyXi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Config, roles, and providers\n2\t\n3\t`src/config/`, `src/cli/config.ts`, `src/cli/resolve.ts`. Credential\n4\tlookup order is in `auth.md`.\n5\t\n6\t## Loading\n7\t\n8\t- `loadConfig(path)` parses `.roast.json` as JSONC with exact-case keys\n9\t  and unknown keys rejected. `version: 1` is required; a literal\n10\t  `api_key` is rejected. There are no built-in roles or models: a role\n11\t  missing from the config fails in `resolveRole`.\n12\t- `jsonc.ts` parses into null-prototype objects (`newObject` /\n13\t  `setKey`, so `__proto__` is an ordinary key). `schema.ts` (zod) checks\n14\t  shape and types only, and `load.ts` keeps the validated *input*, never\n15\t  zod's output (zod's record output turns a `__proto__` key into a\n16\t  prototype). Range and cross-field checks are plain functions in\n17\t  `load.ts` so the Go-era check order holds.\n18\t- `findConfig(start, stop)` walks up to `stop` (the Git toplevel),\n19\t  comparing directories after `realpath`: macOS temp dirs are\n20\t  `/var/...` while `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` prints\n21\t  `/private/var/...`.\n22\t- The CLI loads config only through `loadProjectConfig(explicit, ctx)`\n23\t  (`src/cli/config.ts`), which attaches the stored-credentials store. A\n24\t  missing config is a usage error naming `npx roast init`.\n25\t- Relative prompt-override paths resolve against the config file's\n26\t  directory: read prompts through `promptPath(cfg, ...)`, never the raw\n27\t  config string. The trust projection hashes the raw string, so\n28\t  approvals survive worktree moves.\n29\t\n30\t## Settings\n31\t\n32\tOnly credentials come from outside the config. Every other setting is\n33\tin it (`limits`, `interactive`, `gate`, `review.snapshot`); an explicit\n34\t0 differs from unset, and `load.ts` checks ranges. The CLI resolves\n35\tthem with `flagOrConfigInt` / `flagOrConfigDuration` (`resolve.ts`:\n36\tflag, then config, then default).\n37\t\n38\t## Schema and starter\n39\t\n40\t- `roast.schema.json` (repo root, shipped through `package.json`\n41\t  `files`) is generated: `npm run schema` renders\n42\t  `src/config/json-schema.ts` from the zod schema. Adding, removing, or\n43\t  retyping a config field changes the zod schema and the config types\n44\t  in the same change, then regenerates; never edit the JSON by hand.\n45\t  `test/config/schema.ts` fails on drift. Editor-only constraints (enum,\n46\t  pattern, minimum, required) go in the zod `.meta()`.\n47\t- The `roast init` starter (`starter.ts`) shows commented-out defaults\n48\t  from `defaults.ts`, the same module runtime settings use.\n49\t- `starter()` takes a `RoleChoice` per role (provider + model).\n50\t  `starterFromModels()` is the backward-compat wrapper that maps model\n51\t  strings onto choices via `placeModel` / `otherProvider`.\n52\t  `choiceFromModel()` builds a `RoleChoice` from a flag value.\n53\t- `placeModel` places a model by its ID alone: a\n54\t  `<vendor>/<model>[:<variant>]` ID goes to OpenRouter, a bare ID to the\n55\t  provider `inferFamily` names. A placeholder role follows an OpenRouter\n56\t  role onto OpenRouter; otherwise it takes the other direct provider.\n57\t- Suggested model IDs for each built-in provider live in\n58\t  `SUGGESTED_MODELS` (`defaults.ts`). The `UnplaceableModelError`\n59\t  example text uses them so the two cannot drift.\n60\t\n61\t## Providers\n62\t\n63\t- `lookupProvider(name)` and `providerAt(endpoint, protocol)`\n64\t  (`provider.ts`) are the one place that says which endpoint,\n65\t  protocols, standard key variable, key page, and login method a\n66\t  provider has. Trust standardness, ambient credentials, and the `init`\n67\t  starter consult it; add a provider there, not in those callers. A\n68\t  provider's first protocol is the one starter profiles use.\n69\t- A new provider's key variable must be stripped from test\n70\t  environments: see `cleanEnv` in `typescript.md`.\n71\t- `defaultBaseURL(protocol)` stays separate: it is the implicit endpoint\n72\t  of a profile that omits one; OpenRouter is never one.\n73\t- A role that gets no ambient key reports any set provider key variable\n74\t  as withheld (`withheldKey`, `credential.ts`), preferring the\n75\t  protocol's default provider.\n76\t- `parseEndpoint` (`provider.ts`) is the one endpoint parser (treats\n77\t  `https:///v1` and `https:v1` as an empty host); `endpoint.ts` and\n78\t  `sameEndpoint` use it.\n79\t\n80\t## Roles (`role.ts`, `credential.ts`, `provider.ts`)\n81\t\n82\t- Resolution takes `env` explicitly and never reads `process.env`.\n83\t- `ResolvedRole` is frozen with a non-enumerable `apiKey` and `stored`,\n84\t  so JSON, spread, and `util.inspect` omit the secret. Change a role\n85\t  with `updateRole(role, changes)`; a `{...role}` spread drops the key.\n86\t- `StoredCredentials` lives in `credential.ts` (re-exported by\n87\t  `load.ts`).\n88\t\n89\t## Tests\n90\t\n91\t- Role tests build configs with `configFrom` / `resolveFinder` and the\n92\t  in-memory `FakeStore` in `test/config/helpers.ts`.\n93\t- Configs the tests load as realistic examples go in\n94\t  `test/config/examples.ts`; the schema test validates each with ajv.\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"814e505e-c3f6-40bd-873f-c494d2caa400","uuid":"f3f28618-cb80-4f89-9dcd-054cb65e54ef","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:44:39.427Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-02-builtin-provider-prompts/docs/agents/config.md","content":"# Config, roles, and providers\n\n`src/config/`, `src/cli/config.ts`, `src/cli/resolve.ts`. Credential\nlookup order is in `auth.md`.\n\n## Loading\n\n- `loadConfig(path)` parses `.roast.json` as JSONC with exact-case keys\n  and unknown keys rejected. `version: 1` is required; a literal\n  `api_key` is rejected. There are no built-in roles or models: a role\n  missing from the config fails in `resolveRole`.\n- `jsonc.ts` parses into null-prototype objects (`newObject` /\n  `setKey`, so `__proto__` is an ordinary key). `schema.ts` (zod) checks\n  shape and types only, and `load.ts` keeps the validated *input*, never\n  zod's output (zod's record output turns a `__proto__` key into a\n  prototype). Range and cross-field checks are plain functions in\n  `load.ts` so the Go-era check order holds.\n- `findConfig(start, stop)` walks up to `stop` (the Git toplevel),\n  comparing directories after `realpath`: macOS temp dirs are\n  `/var/...` while `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` prints\n  `/private/var/...`.\n- The CLI loads config only through `loadProjectConfig(explicit, ctx)`\n  (`src/cli/config.ts`), which attaches the stored-credentials store. A\n  missing config is a usage error naming `npx roast init`.\n- Relative prompt-override paths resolve against the config file's\n  directory: read prompts through `promptPath(cfg, ...)`, never the raw\n  config string. The trust projection hashes the raw string, so\n  approvals survive worktree moves.\n\n## Settings\n\nOnly credentials come from outside the config. Every other setting is\nin it (`limits`, `interactive`, `gate`, `review.snapshot`); an explicit\n0 differs from unset, and `load.ts` checks ranges. The CLI resolves\nthem with `flagOrConfigInt` / `flagOrConfigDuration` (`resolve.ts`:\nflag, then config, then default).\n\n## Schema and starter\n\n- `roast.schema.json` (repo root, shipped through `package.json`\n  `files`) is generated: `npm run schema` renders\n  `src/config/json-schema.ts` from the zod schema. Adding, removing, or\n  retyping a config field changes the zod schema and the config types\n  in the same change, then regenerates; never edit the JSON by hand.\n  `test/config/schema.ts` fails on drift. Editor-only constraints (enum,\n  pattern, minimum, required) go in the zod `.meta()`.\n- The `roast init` starter (`starter.ts`) shows commented-out defaults\n  from `defaults.ts`, the same module runtime settings use.\n- `starter()` takes a `RoleChoice` per role (provider + model).\n  `starterFromModels()` is the backward-compat wrapper that maps model\n  strings onto choices via `placeModel` / `otherProvider`.\n  `choiceFromModel()` builds a `RoleChoice` from a flag value.\n- `placeModel` places a model by its ID alone: a\n  `<vendor>/<model>[:<variant>]` ID goes to OpenRouter, a bare ID to the\n  provider `inferFamily` names. A placeholder role follows an OpenRouter\n  role onto OpenRouter; otherwise it takes the other direct provider.\n- Suggested model IDs for each built-in provider live in\n  `SUGGESTED_MODELS` (`defaults.ts`). The `UnplaceableModelError`\n  example text uses them so the two cannot drift.\n\n## Providers\n\n- `lookupProvider(name)` and `providerAt(endpoint, protocol)`\n  (`provider.ts`) are the one place that says which endpoint,\n  protocols, standard key variable, key page, and login method a\n  provider has. Trust standardness, ambient credentials, and the `init`\n  starter consult it; add a provider there, not in those callers. A\n  provider's first protocol is the one starter profiles use.\n- A new provider's key variable must be stripped from test\n  environments: see `cleanEnv` in `typescript.md`.\n- `defaultBaseURL(protocol)` stays separate: it is the implicit endpoint\n  of a profile that omits one; OpenRouter is never one.\n- A role that gets no ambient key reports any set provider key variable\n  as withheld (`withheldKey`, `credential.ts`), preferring the\n  protocol's default provider.\n- `parseEndpoint` (`provider.ts`) is the one endpoint parser (treats\n  `https:///v1` and `https:v1` as an empty host); `endpoint.ts` and\n  `sameEndpoint` use it.\n\n## Roles (`role.ts`, `credential.ts`, `provider.ts`)\n\n- Resolution takes `env` explicitly and never reads `process.env`.\n- `ResolvedRole` is frozen with a non-enumerable `apiKey` and `stored`,\n  so JSON, spread, and `util.inspect` omit the secret. Change a role\n  with `updateRole(role, changes)`; a `{...role}` spread drops the key.\n- `StoredCredentials` lives in `credential.ts` (re-exported by\n  `load.ts`).\n\n## Tests\n\n- Role tests build configs with `configFrom` / `resolveFinder` and the\n  in-memory `FakeStore` in `test/config/helpers.ts`.\n- Configs the tests load as realistic examples go in\n  `test/config/examples.ts`; the schema test validates each with ajv.\n","numLines":95,"startLine":1,"totalLines":95}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PdGq1Hck5V1DxeVoLUvyXi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
