{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011ChNVRzAVcVjoeWtNW2GfL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's the \"init succeeds after three rejected keys\" test. The credentials don't have \"Bearer \" prefix now. That's because with model flags the roles change -- with `--finder-model claude-opus-5-5 --verifier-model gpt-5`, the first login offer is for Anthropic (paste login, which uses `x-api-key` header, not `Bearer`), and the second is for OpenAI (which uses `Bearer`). Previously without model flags, placeholders were used and the providers were openai (finder) and anthropic (verifier). Now the credential format changed because of the provider order.\n\nLet me fix these existing test assertions by switching to the correct model flag order. The original tests had openai first then anthropic (from placeholder ordering). With `--finder-model claude-opus-5-5` the finder is anthropic, verifier is openai. The key check for anthropic uses `x-api-key` header (no Bearer prefix), openai uses `Authorization: Bearer`.\n\nLet me adjust the model flags and expected results:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":96528,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":341},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"814e505e-c3f6-40bd-873f-c494d2caa400","uuid":"8175beff-c6c7-4a2b-82a4-086612899839","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:49:46.429Z","request_id":"req_011ChNVRz5Y4dHAQWda7fxtu"}
