{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016HcQVfqErWZuHEC5h6tiDx","type":"tool_result","content":"68\t### 2. Create the project config\n69\t\n70\t```sh\n71\tnpx roast init\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\tThis writes `.roast.json` in the current directory and adds `/.roast/` to\n75\t`.gitignore`. Command `init` picks each role's provider from its\n76\tmodel ID:\n77\t\n78\t- a bare Claude model ID (`claude-opus-5-5`) uses Anthropic's Messages API\n79\t- a bare OpenAI model ID (including Codex, `gpt-6.1-terra`) uses OpenAI's\n80\t  Responses API\n81\t- a slash-form ID, `<vendor>/<model>` with an optional `:<variant>`\n82\t  (`anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`, `meta-llama/llama-4:free`), uses\n83\t  [OpenRouter](#openrouter).\n84\t\n85\tEither model can fill either role. It's recommended to use models from different \n86\tproviders for each role. For a model that no built-in provider serves,\n87\tedit `.roast.json` by hand (see [Project config](#project-config)).\n88\tWithout the flags, `init` writes placeholder model IDs,\n89\tand a review refuses to run until you replace them in `.roast.json`.\n90\t\n91\tIn the terminal, `init` then offers to log in to each provider\n92\tthat has no credential yet (see [Login and logout](#login-and-logout)).\n93\t\n94\tFlag `--no-login` skips the login process.\n95\t\n96\t\n97\t#### `init` Example\n98\t\n99\tClaude as the finder and Codex as the verifier:\n100\t\n101\t```sh\n102\tnpx roast init --finder-model 'claude-opus-5-5' \\\n103\t  --verifier-model 'gpt-6.1-terra'\n104\t```\n105\t\n106\t`init` refuses to overwrite an existing `.roast.json`.\n107\t\n108\t\n109\t### 3. Login\n110\t\n111\tIf you skipped the login process during `init`, log in now:\n112\t\n113\t```sh\n114\tnpx roast login\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\tWith no argument, `login` reads `.roast.json` and logs in to each built-in"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015u2svpT9517kX23JxpcCpc","agent_id":"a8ed79bc4c0d733b9","session_id":"814e505e-c3f6-40bd-873f-c494d2caa400","uuid":"6eeb4f3f-bafd-47db-a1e6-836ba5046de4","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:52:54.512Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016HcQVfqErWZuHEC5h6tiDx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"fork","task_description":"Read doc files for updates"}
