{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016ELEViYznUSVhKSpdUx9Eg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Packaging, build, and release\n2\t\n3\t`package.json`, `scripts/`, `tsconfig*.json`. Spec:\n4\t`.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/15-packaging.md`.\n5\t\n6\t## The package\n7\t\n8\t- One pure-JS package. `bin.roast` is `dist/cli.js`, a single esbuild\n9\t  ESM bundle. `files` lists exact paths, so build by-products such as\n10\t  `dist/meta.json` never ship.\n11\t- `dependencies` stays empty and there is no `optionalDependencies`,\n12\t  `main`, or `exports`: anything in `dependencies` installs into every\n13\t  user's project. Runtime libraries (`yargs`, `zod`, `jsonc-parser`) are\n14\t  `devDependencies` that the bundle inlines.\n15\t- `roast.schema.json` stays at the package root: `init` writes a\n16\t  `$schema` of `node_modules/@substrate-system/roast/roast.schema.json`.\n17\t- `os` is `darwin`/`linux` and `engines.node` is `>=22.18`;\n18\t  `@types/node` tracks that major so code cannot use a newer API.\n19\t- `overrides.typescript` (`$typescript`) lets npm install typescript-eslint,\n20\t  whose `typescript` peer range stops below 7, without `--force`; lint\n21\t  still runs eslint against the TypeScript 6 API\n22\t  (`scripts/eslint-ts6.ts`). Drop both once typescript-eslint accepts\n23\t  TypeScript 7. Test installs without `force`: an `npm_config_force`\n24\t  in the shell hides a broken resolution.\n25\t- There is no committed lockfile (`package-lock=false` is the whole npm\n26\t  config). CI writes one with `npm install --package-lock-only\n27\t  --package-lock=true` before `npm ci`, which refuses to run without it.\n28\t\n29\t## Build\n30\t\n31\t- `npm run build` runs `npm run schema`, then `scripts/bundle.ts`: it\n32\t  recreates `dist/`, bundles `src/cli.ts`, writes `dist/meta.json` and\n33\t  `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`, and makes `dist/cli.js` executable.\n34\t  Version, commit, and date are injected through esbuild `define`s; the\n35\t  test bundle has none, so it reports `dev`.\n36\t- Text assets (prompt templates under `src/prompts/templates/`,\n37\t  `src/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`, `src/gate/pre-commit.sh`) are\n38\t  imported as strings through the text loader. `test/tooling/assets.ts`\n39\t  checks each one equals its file.\n40\t- `npm run schema` regenerates `roast.schema.json` from the zod schema;\n41\t  CI fails on an uncommitted change to it.\n42\t- Build before `npx roast` in this repo: it resolves the root package's\n43\t  own bin, and with no executable `dist/cli.js` a `roast` on `PATH` (for\n44\t  example Homebrew) can answer instead.\n45\t\n46\t## Checks and release\n47\t\n48\t- `npm run check:pack` (`scripts/check-pack.ts`, after a build) dry-run\n49\t  packs the package and fails unless the tarball lists every required\n50\t  file, the manifest has a `license` and no dependencies, and\n51\t  `dist/cli.js` has the shebang and owner execute bit. It runs on\n52\t  `process.cwd()`, so `test/tooling/check-pack.ts` runs it in fixtures.\n53\t  npm 12 prints `npm pack --json` as an object keyed by package name,\n54\t  older npm as an array.\n55\t- Release is local, through the npm lifecycle: `npm version <x>` runs\n56\t  lint (`preversion`), updates the README toc and `CHANGELOG.md`\n57\t  (`auto-changelog`), commits and tags, then `postversion` pushes and\n58\t  publishes; `prepublishOnly` builds and runs `check:pack`. A failing\n59\t  `prepublishOnly` after the tag is pushed is fixed by a follow-up patch\n60\t  release, never by re-tagging.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015u2svpT9517kX23JxpcCpc","agent_id":"a8ed79bc4c0d733b9","session_id":"814e505e-c3f6-40bd-873f-c494d2caa400","uuid":"e4547ed6-fba3-42ec-a9cb-fd76994be37e","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:52:58.963Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016ELEViYznUSVhKSpdUx9Eg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"fork","task_description":"Read doc files for updates"}
