{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UCBGuB9NgQFEdwuXobKMMP","type":"tool_result","content":"65\tnpm i -D @substrate-system/roast\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\t### 2. Create the project config\n69\t\n70\t```sh\n71\tnpx roast init\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\tThis writes `.roast.json` in the current directory and adds `/.roast/` to\n75\t`.gitignore`. Command `init` picks each role's provider from its\n76\tmodel ID:\n77\t\n78\t- a bare Claude model ID (`claude-opus-5-5`) uses Anthropic's Messages API\n79\t- a bare OpenAI model ID (including Codex, `gpt-6.1-terra`) uses OpenAI's\n80\t  Responses API\n81\t- a slash-form ID, `<vendor>/<model>` with an optional `:<variant>`\n82\t  (`anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`, `meta-llama/llama-4:free`), uses\n83\t  [OpenRouter](#openrouter).\n84\t\n85\tEither model can fill either role. It's recommended to use models from different \n86\tproviders for each role. For a model that no built-in provider serves,\n87\tedit `.roast.json` by hand (see [Project config](#project-config)).\n88\tWithout the flags, `init` writes placeholder model IDs,\n89\tand a review refuses to run until you replace them in `.roast.json`.\n90\t\n91\tIn the terminal, `init` then offers to log in to each provider\n92\tthat has no credential yet (see [Login and logout](#login-and-logout)).\n93\t\n94\tFlag `--no-login` skips the login process.\n95\t\n96\t\n97\t#### `init` Example\n98\t\n99\tClaude as the finder and Codex as the verifier:\n100\t\n101\t```sh\n102\tnpx roast init --finder-model 'claude-opus-5-5' \\\n103\t  --verifier-model 'gpt-6.1-terra'\n104\t```\n105\t\n106\t`init` refuses to overwrite an existing `.roast.json`.\n107\t\n108\t\n109\t### 3. Login\n110\t\n111\tIf you skipped the login process during `init`, log in now:\n112\t\n113\t```sh\n114\tnpx roast login"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"814e505e-c3f6-40bd-873f-c494d2caa400","uuid":"5056d25d-3242-4625-982b-14102b4038d5","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:53:13.856Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-02-builtin-provider-prompts/README.md","content":"npm i -D @substrate-system/roast\n```\n\n### 2. Create the project config\n\n```sh\nnpx roast init\n```\n\nThis writes `.roast.json` in the current directory and adds `/.roast/` to\n`.gitignore`. Command `init` picks each role's provider from its\nmodel ID:\n\n- a bare Claude model ID (`claude-opus-5-5`) uses Anthropic's Messages API\n- a bare OpenAI model ID (including Codex, `gpt-6.1-terra`) uses OpenAI's\n  Responses API\n- a slash-form ID, `<vendor>/<model>` with an optional `:<variant>`\n  (`anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`, `meta-llama/llama-4:free`), uses\n  [OpenRouter](#openrouter).\n\nEither model can fill either role. It's recommended to use models from different \nproviders for each role. For a model that no built-in provider serves,\nedit `.roast.json` by hand (see [Project config](#project-config)).\nWithout the flags, `init` writes placeholder model IDs,\nand a review refuses to run until you replace them in `.roast.json`.\n\nIn the terminal, `init` then offers to log in to each provider\nthat has no credential yet (see [Login and logout](#login-and-logout)).\n\nFlag `--no-login` skips the login process.\n\n\n#### `init` Example\n\nClaude as the finder and Codex as the verifier:\n\n```sh\nnpx roast init --finder-model 'claude-opus-5-5' \\\n  --verifier-model 'gpt-6.1-terra'\n```\n\n`init` refuses to overwrite an existing `.roast.json`.\n\n\n### 3. Login\n\nIf you skipped the login process during `init`, log in now:\n\n```sh\nnpx roast login","numLines":50,"startLine":65,"totalLines":647}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UCBGuB9NgQFEdwuXobKMMP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
