{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G4Ff3UyyXowTMPQtDz5hM7","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t- LLM adapters and the agent loop (`src/llm/`): `docs/agents/llm.md`\n41\t- The bundle, third-party notices, `check:pack`, release\n42\t  (`scripts/`, `package.json`): `docs/agents/packaging.md`\n43\t\n44\tA new note goes in its area's file; a new area gets a file and a line\n45\there. This file holds only what most tasks hit.\n46\t\n47\t## Traps every task hits\n48\t\n49\t- `JSON.parse` syntax errors can quote the input. Credential-file parse\n50\t  errors must use value-free messages so diagnostic output cannot expose\n51\t  a stored key.\n52\t- Shell hooks block Bash commands that contain a heredoc mentioning\n53\t  `process.env.PATH`, a heredoc or command containing `env:` or `.env`\n54\t  text, or a `credentials*` path together with `cat`, `sed`, `head`, and\n55\t  the like. Read and write such files with the editor tools.\n56\t- Tests that write project state (run records, trust, stored\n57\t  credentials) chdir into a temporary Git repository first. `.roast/`\n58\t  ignores itself, so a leak into this checkout is invisible to\n59\t  `git status`; check with `ls -a`.\n60\t- CLI diagnostic tests that resolve roles need valid test credentials\n61\t  and local fake-server routing, even when asserting only local checks.\n62\t  Doctor fakes must route GET models checks and POST inference separately;\n63\t  a successful chat probe needs a lookup call followed by a final call\n64\t  that echoes the token from the replayed tool result.\n65\t- The CLI parser preserves dashed option names and disables boolean\n66\t  negation. Declare flags such as `no-browser` explicitly and read\n67\t  `args['no-browser']`, rather than a camel-case property.\n68\t- `simulateTerminals` only bypasses interactive-terminal detection. To\n69\t  exercise raw-mode prompt input through the CLI, give stdin an `isTTY`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8