{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011ChNW7jKPzwoa1NKf6qkD4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now update the notes file:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":121469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":338},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"814e505e-c3f6-40bd-873f-c494d2caa400","uuid":"812b624d-9410-4f00-bbc7-ee45c6c05772","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:58:39.577Z","request_id":"req_011ChNW7jEBxnnoAxNxYkHm7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011ChNW7jKPzwoa1NKf6qkD4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PHmo7ZrKuLDkFfaPFaJWqz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-02-builtin-provider-prompts/.redeye/notes.md","content":"# Ticket 02: Interactive provider and model prompts for built-in providers\n\n## Implemented\n\n### Files changed\n- `src/cli/init.ts` -- added `PROVIDER_MENU`, `suggestedModel()`,\n  `defaultProvider()`, `parseProviderInput()`, `promptProvider()`,\n  `promptModel()`, `promptRoleChoice()`, `writeStarterFromChoices()`.\n  Handler now branches on interactive/non-interactive: prompts when\n  flags missing + interactive, writes placeholders + hint otherwise.\n- `test/cli/init.ts` -- added tests for all 11 checklist items.\n  Updated existing login-offer tests to pass model flags so they don't\n  consume stdin through the new prompts.\n- `README.md` -- updated init section with interactive prompt docs.\n- `docs/agents/config.md` -- added prompt flow description.\n- `docs/agents/packaging.md` -- added release checklist entry.\n- `AGENTS.md` -- added trap about init login tests needing model flags.\n\n### Checklist\n- [x] Choosing each built-in provider by number and accepting the\n      suggested model writes a config whose role resolves onto that\n      provider with the suggested model\n- [x] Choosing a provider by name and typing a model writes that model on\n      that provider\n- [x] Accepting the verifier's default provider after choosing a finder\n      provider places the verifier on the other provider (Anthropic and\n      OpenAI swap; OpenRouter stays OpenRouter)\n- [x] With `--finder-model` given, only the verifier is prompted, and the\n      finder uses the flag's model\n- [x] With both model flags, `init` reads nothing from stdin and writes\n      the flag models\n- [x] Without interactive terminals, `init` writes placeholder models,\n      reads no stdin, and exits successfully\n- [x] An invalid menu choice followed by a valid one succeeds\n- [x] A model that does not place onto the chosen provider (for example an\n      OpenAI ID under Anthropic) followed by a valid one succeeds\n- [x] EOF partway through the prompts exits without writing `.roast.json`,\n      a `.gitignore` entry, or stored credentials\n- [x] An existing `.roast.json` is refused before any stdin is read\n- [x] After the prompts, the login offer still stores a credential for a\n      built-in provider that lacks one\n\n### Key decisions\n- `PROVIDER_MENU` is hardcoded with spec order (Anthropic, OpenAI,\n  OpenRouter) rather than using `builtinProviders()` registry order\n  (which is openai, anthropic, openrouter).\n- `writeStarterFromChoices()` accepts `RoleChoice` directly and calls\n  `starter()`, while `writeStarter()` is kept for the flag-only path\n  using `starterFromModels()`.\n- The handler has two branches: interactive (prompts then\n  `writeStarterFromChoices`) and non-interactive (flags then\n  `writeStarter`). The non-interactive hint is printed to stderr.\n- Existing login-offer tests were updated to pass model flags to avoid\n  the new prompts consuming their stdin.\n- Same-model note is printed to stderr after both prompts.\n\n### Notes for next attempt\n- The `suggestedModel()` for OpenRouter picks the slug for the vendor\n  the other role is NOT using. When the verifier is not yet known,\n  it defaults to the Anthropic slug.\n- `promptModel` validates using `placeModel()` and checks the placed\n  provider matches the chosen provider. This means custom/unknown\n  model IDs that don't place via `placeModel` are rejected at built-in\n  provider prompts, which is per spec.\n- The EOF handling works because `readLine()` returns `null` on EOF,\n  and `promptProvider`/`promptModel` propagate null through\n  `promptRoleChoice`, causing the handler to return early without\n  writing anything.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":121469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":338},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"814e505e-c3f6-40bd-873f-c494d2caa400","uuid":"f509d3c4-10da-4532-b58a-3ead4237563d","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:59:04.636Z","request_id":"req_011ChNW7jEBxnnoAxNxYkHm7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PHmo7ZrKuLDkFfaPFaJWqz":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-02-builtin-provider-prompts/.redeye/notes.md","content":"# Ticket 02: Interactive provider and model prompts for built-in providers\n\n## Implemented\n\n### Files changed\n- `src/cli/init.ts` -- added `PROVIDER_MENU`, `suggestedModel()`,\n  `defaultProvider()`, `parseProviderInput()`, `promptProvider()`,\n  `promptModel()`, `promptRoleChoice()`, `writeStarterFromChoices()`.\n  Handler now branches on interactive/non-interactive: prompts when\n  flags missing + interactive, writes placeholders + hint otherwise.\n- `test/cli/init.ts` -- added tests for all 11 checklist items.\n  Updated existing login-offer tests to pass model flags so they don't\n  consume stdin through the new prompts.\n- `README.md` -- updated init section with interactive prompt docs.\n- `docs/agents/config.md` -- added prompt flow description.\n- `docs/agents/packaging.md` -- added release checklist entry.\n- `AGENTS.md` -- added trap about init login tests needing model flags.\n\n### Checklist\n- [x] Choosing each built-in provider by number and accepting the\n      suggested model writes a config whose role resolves onto that\n      provider with the suggested model\n- [x] Choosing a provider by name and typing a model writes that model on\n      that provider\n- [x] Accepting the verifier's default provider after choosing a finder\n      provider places the verifier on the other provider (Anthropic and\n      OpenAI swap; OpenRouter stays OpenRouter)\n- [x] With `--finder-model` given, only the verifier is prompted, and the\n      finder uses the flag's model\n- [x] With both model flags, `init` reads nothing from stdin and writes\n      the flag models\n- [x] Without interactive terminals, `init` writes placeholder models,\n      reads no stdin, and exits successfully\n- [x] An invalid menu choice followed by a valid one succeeds\n- [x] A model that does not place onto the chosen provider (for example an\n      OpenAI ID under Anthropic) followed by a valid one succeeds\n- [x] EOF partway through the prompts exits without writing `.roast.json`,\n      a `.gitignore` entry, or stored credentials\n- [x] An existing `.roast.json` is refused before any stdin is read\n- [x] After the prompts, the login offer still stores a credential for a\n      built-in provider that lacks one\n\n### Key decisions\n- `PROVIDER_MENU` is hardcoded with spec order (Anthropic, OpenAI,\n  OpenRouter) rather than using `builtinProviders()` registry order\n  (which is openai, anthropic, openrouter).\n- `writeStarterFromChoices()` accepts `RoleChoice` directly and calls\n  `starter()`, while `writeStarter()` is kept for the flag-only path\n  using `starterFromModels()`.\n- The handler has two branches: interactive (prompts then\n  `writeStarterFromChoices`) and non-interactive (flags then\n  `writeStarter`). The non-interactive hint is printed to stderr.\n- Existing login-offer tests were updated to pass model flags to avoid\n  the new prompts consuming their stdin.\n- Same-model note is printed to stderr after both prompts.\n\n### Notes for next attempt\n- The `suggestedModel()` for OpenRouter picks the slug for the vendor\n  the other role is NOT using. When the verifier is not yet known,\n  it defaults to the Anthropic slug.\n- `promptModel` validates using `placeModel()` and checks the placed\n  provider matches the chosen provider. This means custom/unknown\n  model IDs that don't place via `placeModel` are rejected at built-in\n  provider prompts, which is per spec.\n- The EOF handling works because `readLine()` returns `null` on EOF,\n  and `promptProvider`/`promptModel` propagate null through\n  `promptRoleChoice`, causing the handler to return early without\n  writing anything.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PHmo7ZrKuLDkFfaPFaJWqz","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-02-builtin-provider-prompts/.redeye/notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"814e505e-c3f6-40bd-873f-c494d2caa400","uuid":"a47d7868-7534-4547-9ced-3e1d6d5be8df","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:59:05.670Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-02-builtin-provider-prompts/.redeye/notes.md","content":"# Ticket 02: Interactive provider and model prompts for built-in providers\n\n## Implemented\n\n### Files changed\n- `src/cli/init.ts` -- added `PROVIDER_MENU`, `suggestedModel()`,\n  `defaultProvider()`, `parseProviderInput()`, `promptProvider()`,\n  `promptModel()`, `promptRoleChoice()`, `writeStarterFromChoices()`.\n  Handler now branches on interactive/non-interactive: prompts when\n  flags missing + interactive, writes placeholders + hint otherwise.\n- `test/cli/init.ts` -- added tests for all 11 checklist items.\n  Updated existing login-offer tests to pass model flags so they don't\n  consume stdin through the new prompts.\n- `README.md` -- updated init section with interactive prompt docs.\n- `docs/agents/config.md` -- added prompt flow description.\n- `docs/agents/packaging.md` -- added release checklist entry.\n- `AGENTS.md` -- added trap about init login tests needing model flags.\n\n### Checklist\n- [x] Choosing each built-in provider by number and accepting the\n      suggested model writes a config whose role resolves onto that\n      provider with the suggested model\n- [x] Choosing a provider by name and typing a model writes that model on\n      that provider\n- [x] Accepting the verifier's default provider after choosing a finder\n      provider places the verifier on the other provider (Anthropic and\n      OpenAI swap; OpenRouter stays OpenRouter)\n- [x] With `--finder-model` given, only the verifier is prompted, and the\n      finder uses the flag's model\n- [x] With both model flags, `init` reads nothing from stdin and writes\n      the flag models\n- [x] Without interactive terminals, `init` writes placeholder models,\n      reads no stdin, and exits successfully\n- [x] An invalid menu choice followed by a valid one succeeds\n- [x] A model that does not place onto the chosen provider (for example an\n      OpenAI ID under Anthropic) followed by a valid one succeeds\n- [x] EOF partway through the prompts exits without writing `.roast.json`,\n      a `.gitignore` entry, or stored credentials\n- [x] An existing `.roast.json` is refused before any stdin is read\n- [x] After the prompts, the login offer still stores a credential for a\n      built-in provider that lacks one\n\n### Key decisions\n- `PROVIDER_MENU` is hardcoded with spec order (Anthropic, OpenAI,\n  OpenRouter) rather than using `builtinProviders()` registry order\n  (which is openai, anthropic, openrouter).\n- `writeStarterFromChoices()` accepts `RoleChoice` directly and calls\n  `starter()`, while `writeStarter()` is kept for the flag-only path\n  using `starterFromModels()`.\n- The handler has two branches: interactive (prompts then\n  `writeStarterFromChoices`) and non-interactive (flags then\n  `writeStarter`). The non-interactive hint is printed to stderr.\n- Existing login-offer tests were updated to pass model flags to avoid\n  the new prompts consuming their stdin.\n- Same-model note is printed to stderr after both prompts.\n\n### Notes for next attempt\n- The `suggestedModel()` for OpenRouter picks the slug for the vendor\n  the other role is NOT using. When the verifier is not yet known,\n  it defaults to the Anthropic slug.\n- `promptModel` validates using `placeModel()` and checks the placed\n  provider matches the chosen provider. This means custom/unknown\n  model IDs that don't place via `placeModel` are rejected at built-in\n  provider prompts, which is per spec.\n- The EOF handling works because `readLine()` returns `null` on EOF,\n  and `promptProvider`/`promptModel` propagate null through\n  `promptRoleChoice`, causing the handler to return early without\n  writing anything.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":29,"newStart":1,"newLines":68,"lines":[" # Ticket 02: Interactive provider and model prompts for built-in providers"," ","-## Plan","+## Implemented"," ","-The ticket adds interactive prompts to `init` for choosing provider and model","-per role when the model flag is missing. The flow: finder first, then verifier.","-Each asks a provider menu (numbered: Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenRouter), then a","-model prompt with a suggested default.","+### Files changed","+- `src/cli/init.ts` -- added `PROVIDER_MENU`, `suggestedModel()`,","+  `defaultProvider()`, `parseProviderInput()`, `promptProvider()`,","+  `promptModel()`, `promptRoleChoice()`, `writeStarterFromChoices()`.","+  Handler now branches on interactive/non-interactive: prompts when","+  flags missing + interactive, writes placeholders + hint otherwise.","+- `test/cli/init.ts` -- added tests for all 11 checklist items.","+  Updated existing login-offer tests to pass model flags so they don't","+  consume stdin through the new prompts.","+- `README.md` -- updated init section with interactive prompt docs.","+- `docs/agents/config.md` -- added prompt flow description.","+- `docs/agents/packaging.md` -- added release checklist entry.","+- `AGENTS.md` -- added trap about init login tests needing model flags."," ","-### Implementation approach","+### Checklist","+- [x] Choosing each built-in provider by number and accepting the","+      suggested model writes a config whose role resolves onto that","+      provider with the suggested model","+- [x] Choosing a provider by name and typing a model writes that model on","+      that provider","+- [x] Accepting the verifier's default provider after choosing a finder","+      provider places the verifier on the other provider (Anthropic and","+      OpenAI swap; OpenRouter stays OpenRouter)","+- [x] With `--finder-model` given, only the verifier is prompted, and the","+      finder uses the flag's model","+- [x] With both model flags, `init` reads nothing from stdin and writes","+      the flag models","+- [x] Without interactive terminals, `init` writes placeholder models,","+      reads no stdin, and exits successfully","+- [x] An invalid menu choice followed by a valid one succeeds","+- [x] A model that does not place onto the chosen provider (for example an","+      OpenAI ID under Anthropic) followed by a valid one succeeds","+- [x] EOF partway through the prompts exits without writing `.roast.json`,","+      a `.gitignore` entry, or stored credentials","+- [x] An existing `.roast.json` is refused before any stdin is read","+- [x] After the prompts, the login offer still stores a credential for a","+      built-in provider that lacks one"," ","-1. Add a `promptRoleChoice` function in `src/cli/init.ts` that:","-   - Shows a numbered provider menu","-   - Reads provider choice (by number or name)","-   - Shows model prompt with suggested default","-   - Validates model places onto chosen provider","-   - Returns a `RoleChoice`","+### Key decisions","+- `PROVIDER_MENU` is hardcoded with spec order (Anthropic, OpenAI,","+  OpenRouter) rather than using `builtinProviders()` registry order","+  (which is openai, anthropic, openrouter).","+- `writeStarterFromChoices()` accepts `RoleChoice` directly and calls","+  `starter()`, while `writeStarter()` is kept for the flag-only path","+  using `starterFromModels()`.","+- The handler has two branches: interactive (prompts then","+  `writeStarterFromChoices`) and non-interactive (flags then","+  `writeStarter`). The non-interactive hint is printed to stderr.","+- Existing login-offer tests were updated to pass model flags to avoid","+  the new prompts consuming their stdin.","+- Same-model note is printed to stderr after both prompts."," ","-2. Modify the `init` handler to:","-   - Check interactive terminals","-   - For each role missing a model flag, call `promptRoleChoice`","-   - For non-interactive, write placeholders + hint","-   - After all prompts, write starter and offer login as before","-   - Print same-model note when both roles have same model+endpoint+protocol","-","-3. Tests at the CLI seam (in-process via `runRoast` with scripted stdin)","-","-## Progress","-","+### Notes for next attempt","+- The `suggestedModel()` for OpenRouter picks the slug for the vendor","+  the other role is NOT using. When the verifier is not yet known,","+  it defaults to the Anthropic slug.","+- `promptModel` validates using `placeModel()` and checks the placed","+  provider matches the chosen provider. This means custom/unknown","+  model IDs that don't place via `placeModel` are rejected at built-in","+  provider prompts, which is per spec.","+- The EOF handling works because `readLine()` returns `null` on EOF,","+  and `promptProvider`/`promptModel` propagate null through","+  `promptRoleChoice`, causing the handler to return early without","+  writing anything."]}],"originalFile":"# Ticket 02: Interactive provider and model prompts for built-in providers\n\n## Plan\n\nThe ticket adds interactive prompts to `init` for choosing provider and model\nper role when the model flag is missing. The flow: finder first, then verifier.\nEach asks a provider menu (numbered: Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenRouter), then a\nmodel prompt with a suggested default.\n\n### Implementation approach\n\n1. Add a `promptRoleChoice` function in `src/cli/init.ts` that:\n   - Shows a numbered provider menu\n   - Reads provider choice (by number or name)\n   - Shows model prompt with suggested default\n   - Validates model places onto chosen provider\n   - Returns a `RoleChoice`\n\n2. Modify the `init` handler to:\n   - Check interactive terminals\n   - For each role missing a model flag, call `promptRoleChoice`\n   - For non-interactive, write placeholders + hint\n   - After all prompts, write starter and offer login as before\n   - Print same-model note when both roles have same model+endpoint+protocol\n\n3. Tests at the CLI seam (in-process via `runRoast` with scripted stdin)\n\n## Progress\n\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PHmo7ZrKuLDkFfaPFaJWqz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
